<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine analysts hail $2 bln global bond.</title>
<headline>Argentine analysts hail $2 bln global bond.</headline>
<byline>Jason Webb</byline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine bond analysts welcomed Tuesday the government's $2 billion global bond placement as a successful start to its year's hunt for cash and a good argument for lower Argentine spreads.</p>
<p>Joint lead managers J.P. Morgan and Merrill Lynch announced in London that the 20-year bond was priced with a spread of 462.5 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasury bonds.</p>
</text>
